        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2004",
        "question_text": "<p>Express $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x + 2)}$ in partial fractions.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x + 2}$.<br>Multiply through by $(x + 1)(x + 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x + 2) + B(x + 1)$.<br>Set $x = -1$: $3(-1) + 5 = A(1) + B(0) \\Rightarrow 2 = A$.<br>Set $x = -2$: $3(-2) + 5 = A(0) + B(-1) \\Rightarrow -1 = -B \\Rightarrow B = 1$.<br>Thus, $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{2}{x + 1} + \\frac{1}{x + 2}$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
